\section{Stages}{

\code{status} is \code{"ok"}; \code{"failed"}, with the condition message in
\code{message}; \code{"skipped"}, when a stage it reads produced nothing or
\code{refit = "never"} found nothing stored; \code{"stale"}, when \code{refit = "never"} read a result made from other inputs or software versions
than this plan's (the result is kept, but it is not this plan's); or
the plan's own status for a stage that does not run (\code{"not built"},
\code{"not applicable"}, \code{"excluded"}). A failed stage is never an error of
\code{run_validation()}.

The headline is \code{"incomplete"} while a required stage that
exists is not \code{"ok"}; \code{"not validated"} when a required criterion
failed; \code{"not judged"} when none failed but one could not be evaluated
(a response without a known range, say); and \code{"validated"}, printed
with the plan version and hash, only when every required criterion was
evaluated and met.

What each stage runs:
\itemize{
\item \code{run_record}: \code{\link[=run_info]{run_info()}}, written to \verb{<dir>/run-info.rds} before any
other stage and again, with the end row, after the last.
\item \code{prior_predictive}: \code{\link[=prior_check]{prior_check()}} on data simulated at the plan's
prior-check design point, under bmm's default priors and, when the
calibration has its own, under that one too.
\item \code{sbc}: \code{\link[=sbc]{sbc()}} at the plan's design point under the plan's prior.
\item \code{recovery}: \code{\link[=recovery_grid]{recovery_grid()}} over the plan's grid at the population,
SD and subject levels, with the model correlations where there are at
least two subject-varying parameters, every cell gated by
\code{\link[=check_convergence]{check_convergence()}} and contracted against a prior-only fit
(\code{prior_sd = "fit"}).
\item \code{computation}, \code{identifiability}, \code{individual_differences}: tables
read off the recovery grid's cells and summary.
\item \code{data_requirements}: the read-off, \code{\link[=smallest_design]{smallest_design()}} of the
subject-level \code{r_low} along \code{n_trials} at the plan's
\code{read_off_n_subjects}, at \code{read_off_r_low} and at 0.70 and 0.90; one
row per subject-varying parameter and threshold with \code{n_subjects},
\code{term}, \code{threshold}, \code{smallest} and \code{status}. It has no coverage
condition of its own (see \code{\link[=verdict_table]{verdict_table()}}).
\item \code{agreement}: \code{\link[=cross_check]{cross_check()}} of the fit of the largest design's first
replication against the plan's reference.
}
}

\section{Resuming}{

A stage's inputs are the plan fields it reads, its seed, the \code{...} of
the call, the fitter, the versions of bmm, brms, bmmtools, the Stan
toolchain (and SBC for the calibration) and, for a stage read off the
grid, the grid's inputs. They are hashed into the stage's status file,
and a stage is read rather than rerun while its hash is unchanged and
its status is \code{"ok"}, so a new bmm release reruns every stage. A grid
with failed cells is rerun, which retries those cells and reads the
others from their cache, and a stage read off the grid is computed
again whenever the grid was not read. The whole
plan is written to \verb{<dir>/plan.rds}; a plan whose hash differs from
the stored one is announced and replaces it.
}

